# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mali r54p1 EGL config table. NOT tuning, and NOT optional. [C]
#
# The vendor tree will ship Mali r54p1 (Samsung SM-A175F donor, same Mali-G57
# MC2 -- donor ACCEPTED 2026-09-19). At r38p1+ ARM moved the per-format EGL
# config table OUT of the driver into these properties; r32p1 had it compiled
# in, which is why stock sets none. Left unset, the driver rebuilds the table
# from defaults and camera/video GL pipelines get zero eglChooseConfig
# matches (EGL_BAD_CONFIG force-closes -- RS4 27/08 HOTFIX lesson).
#
# STATUS [C]: these 39 values restore the RS4 stock r32p1 table (same GPU
# G57 MC2, same r32p1-01eac0 stock UMD class). The Advan stock table itself
# is UNREAD (needs a running driver -- tester gate below). r54p1 reads 19
# buckets and the YUV set is load-bearing for it (without: 24 configs /
# 6 recordable / camera FAILS; with: 65 / 47 / WORKS -- RS4-measured), so
# the YUV buckets ship here even though their 0x200+ codes are ARM-private.
# Tester gate before release (tools/egl-config-check.sh floor, not row
# equality): RECORDABLE and WINDOW_BIT counts >= Advan stock r32p1's, and
# WhatsApp-class camera OPEN + CAPTURE works.
#
# THE LABEL MATTERS AS MUCH AS THE VALUE: sepolicy/vendor/property_contexts
# must map ro.vendor.arm.* (else vendor_default_prop, unreadable by apps,
# and the driver sees unset). Property-read refusals are dontaudit'd, so no
# denial sweep can ever catch a missing label -- only the functional gate can.
#
ro.vendor.arm.egl.configs.r8_g8_b8_a8_32bit_fixed.hal_format=0x1
ro.vendor.arm.egl.configs.r8_g8_b8_a8_32bit_fixed.recordable=true
ro.vendor.arm.egl.configs.r8_g8_b8_a8_32bit_fixed.framebuffer_target=true
